Z||000013||Cheever2||04-20-2001||01:11 PM||||Hmmm, the 2 places I know best, Oklahoma and Ohio.  The only thing I really liked about Oklahoma was the fishing, forget about it in Ohio & Texas.  Ohio had all the seasons, and there around you guys in the southwest corner I thought was very pretty.  I drove by Caesar Creek Lake every day and that's fairly scenic.  <P>I think you've just had an extremely long winter this year, and you've come to the end of your patience.  Hang in there, the good stuff is almost here.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000014||stimpy||04-20-2001||01:48 PM||||Yep, sqoach, nuthin like a good ol' red mudstorm coming down on a freshly washed car! Also, you know you're in Oklahoma when a good parking spot has nothing to do with proximity to the entrance, but if it's got shade. And who knows when a nice twister will come through and put my Fiero in someone's bathtub. Screw this, I'm going back to California!<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||bHooper||04-20-2001||02:38 PM||||OhiO gets what it deserves for trying to claim that they are "the birthplace of aviation", or whatever   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Lisa, if it makes you feel any better, it was in the 80's all last week, and snowed on tuesday, here!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's<BR>and spellcheck crash's windows<BR>Poly Bushings<BR>Accel Coil||||reg||1
Z||000016||btoth||04-20-2001||03:09 PM||||All I know about Ohio weather is that it sucks.  I walked all the way across campus in the pouring rain to go to class today only to find out it was cancelled... so I had to walk back to where I came from (in the pouring rain) to get to my car.  Then, as soon as I get in the car, the rain stops.  Go fig.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||beer_stud_21||04-20-2001||04:20 PM||||Well we dont get snow here except for the summit of the mountain, but if you wanna talk about rain I have a story for you.  Last November we had 45 inches of rain.  24 of that was in one 24 hour period.  The river flooded, the desert on the other side of the island flooded and washed out the road.  A couple houses got washed away and a crap load of dirt and rocks got washed into downtown hilo.  And even now its been mostly cloudy/rainy for the last 7-8 days.  But daytime temperature is 73-85 EVERY SINGLE DAY.  Which after you've lived here for 10 years gets boring.  I actually like the mainland winter.  And especially HATE the hawaii humidity!  <P>-Marlin||||reg||1
