Z||000021||fiero56||04-20-2001||08:21 PM||||Man...what I wouldn't give for the opportunity to move to Kansas or Oklahoma. I <B>love</B> BIG severe storms, and wide open corn fields as far as I can see(seriously, no joke). I love watching the movie <I>twister</I>, all the storms, and all that flat farmland, that's where I want to be.<P>Oh yea, Hoop, you better watch it with your "First in Flight" plates <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Everyone knows you guys wouldn't have that title if us Daytonians weren't so damn inventive(electric starter, pop can top  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, even played a part in development of nuclear bomb trigger). And I drive by the Wright's Bike shop almost daily.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Eric||04-21-2001||12:45 AM||||Is the shop still there?  <P>The only thing worse than rainy weather is high winds.  I believe that is the reason the Wrights chose Kitty Hawk; they could bank on a consistant headwind.  Of course, every time they needed to fix a broken part, they had to go back to Ohio.  Isn't that a song too?||||reg||1
Z||000023||Tweek||04-21-2001||12:57 AM||||I live in Maine. And thats all I have to say about that.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Wade87GT||04-21-2001||01:16 AM||||Tweek, I recently read something, somewhere that listed the ten best drives. The whole coast of Maine was in there! Man, am I overdue for a New England clam boil.<P>Wade||||reg||14
Z||000025||voyagerspe||04-21-2001||01:33 AM||||Learn to ski, get a snowboard, get a snowmobile.  Enjoy everyday of the year.  Its  great to have 4 seasons there is something to do in each.  As for the rain, id rather have it raining then have my state on fire (sorry Florida).||||reg||14
Z||000026||rogergarrison||04-21-2001||07:07 AM||||I lived in Tulsa and Okla City for 6 years, I personnaly liked the weather. 9-10 months of summer 2-3 winter. Only an occational sleet storm. We used to sit on patio and watch for tornados. Dont let people tell you that in thier state 'if you dont like the weather,wait a minute and itll change'. Ive heard that in every single state ive ever been in. About Maine, isnt there a Mt Washington or something there that has the worse weather on earth except for Antartica?||||reg||1
Z||000027||fiero56||04-21-2001||07:29 AM||||Yup, the shop is still there(its on South Williams street), so is the building they used for their printing business, but I don't know where in town it is. Both buildings are now owned by the National Park Service. There is talk going on about restoring the printing shop over the next few years. I hear its not in the best part of town and is pretty run-down...<P>There might not be a whole lot I like about Ohio, but the Dayton area isn't too bad to live in, lots of colleges to choose from, lots and lots of tech jobs, good schools, but I can't wait to leave either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000028||Cameron||04-21-2001||11:20 PM||||Ya...well Ohio may suck, but to oppose popular belief, California SUCKS MORE!  I hate it here in Cali.  Yes the weather is good.  Well, moderate at best.  We don't have seasons.  It is either Sunny or Raining.  Now what is that.  And it can change from sunny to raining overnight.  But that isn't even the bad part.  The part that sucks is it is SO <B>crowded</B> that you are either in traffic or are worried that a drunk driver or an idiot will destroy you and your beautiful Fiero.  I work in the internet business and yes it may be the center of the silicon valley and that just makes it worse.  I eventually want to own a lot of land with horses and a huge garage to work on my Fiero, and that doesn't exist in Cali.  You can't find much land out here and if you can there is no way in hell that it is affordable.  You would have to be a billionaire to afford it.  And there are hardly and Fiero shows...That I must say is the worst part.  I have to drive 2000-3000 miles for the good shows.  That is a bunch of crap.  I'm moving out of here as soon as I can find a job in the mid-west.<P>Oh well, thanks for hearing me rant.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000029||Slammed Fiero||04-22-2001||12:03 AM||||Don't forget those Ohio Pot holes lisa....<P>or as I like to call them tracer killers...<BR>hah<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000030||DJRice||04-22-2001||09:57 PM||||Two seasons in Ohio:  Winter & Construction<P>Things have been nice in Florida so far no doubt.  You have to love the smell of burnt underbrush in the morning.  I enjoy quality time with my Fiero while dusting off the ash!<P>Looks like the latest round of fires on the east side of the state were started by some pyro.  <P>Stimpy, <P>As long as your not parking your car near trailer parks, you shouldnt have to worry about the whole bathtub thing....<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000031||Cheever2||04-22-2001||10:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR>We used to sit on patio and watch for tornados.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>The first 29 years of my life I lived in Tulsa, and never once saw a tornado.  Sure tried.  I would drive like a maniac trying to get to them.  One friend was at a Burger King when a tornado came, they went into the walk-in freezer, and that was all that was left when it was over (they had trouble getting the door open because of the debris).  My aunt had twin twisters go on each side of her house and damaged her neighbor's houses but not hers - one of those proceeded over a church where we knew the pastor.  He went under his big oak desk, and again, it was the only thing left.<P>Once saw a funnel cloud in Ohio, which later took the roof off a barn.  Big deal.  Maybe I'll see a hurricane here in Houston.<P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000032||FieroLisa||04-22-2001||10:49 PM||||Jonathan: I admire your pothole-avoiding ability, I mean you could have blown more than 2 tires, right??......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DJRice- I was just commenting about the construction in Ohio today- might as well call it the Orange Barrel State!||||reg||1
Z||000033||tgowens||04-23-2001||03:13 AM||||Lisa, orange barrels are the state flower, they pop up every spring!||||reg||1
Z||000034||kslish||04-23-2001||07:09 AM||||About those orange cones....at least Ohio attempts to repair their roads.  Pennsylvania on the other hand seems to wait till they completely fall apart before doing anything.  They had to shut down part of the Turnpike this weekend because one of the overpasses started to buckle under it's own weight!!  The highways here are in particularly bad shape this year with the longer than usual winter. <P>However, Ohio could quit sending their lousy weather our way.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000035||Formula88||04-24-2001||12:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>Lisa, orange barrels are the state flower, they pop up every spring!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's also true about NC.  But on a return trip from FL one year, I knew I was back in the middle of the South when I saw one of the light up billboard type road contruction signs that read, "Drive with caution, Road being doctored."<P>It's weird.  FL is less southern than NC!  And central FL is about as far south as you can go without HAVING to speek Spanish.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But boy, do I miss Cocoa Beach.  Especially now that I know about all the Fiero happenings down there.  Didn't have my beast when I lived there. ||||reg||1
